{"name":"Desert Tan","hex":"#a38c6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"desert","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barren area of land or desolate terrain, especially one with little water or vegetation; a wasteland.\n\nIn particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground.","In particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Usually of a place: abandoned, deserted, or uninhabited."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)","wikidata":"Q1670336"},{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_sou